From 438349dc83c07fe5c10ec53ecc62ab54636090b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Feder <noreply@splitmind.invalid>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:01:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(catalog): label actions that write as write or
 destructive

Read-only connections, and the read-only MCP consent grants, trust each
action's operationType. These actions were labelled read although they
mutate state, sign write or delete URLs, consume one-time state, or may
leave files in the account:

destructive: aws_s3.generate_presigned_url, aliyun_oss.generate_presigned_url
(both can sign a DELETE).

write: cloudflare_r2.generate_presigned_url, tailscale.rotate_webhook_secret,
pinata.pin_by_cid, keygen.ping_machine, keygen.ping_process,
mailgun.verify_domain, vercel.verify_project_domain, msg91.verify_otp,
myotp_app.verify_otp, fusion-api.file_upload_generate_presigned_url and
..._urls, harpa_ai.run_ai_prompt, and fuxin.create_pdf_from_document,
create_pdf_from_html, merge_documents, remove_password_from_document.
The last few are uncertain, so they fail closed.

Billed but non-mutating actions (LLM completions, embeddings, screenshots)
stay read. Adds a catalog test for every label and Worker tests that a
read-only aws_s3 connection refuses a presigned URL.
